{"id": "EUVD-2026-86698", "enisaUuid": "158c0117-08b7-38ee-a6f5-511dcbfdb8f5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark faultable stack helpers as sleepable\n\nThe faultable variants of bpf_get_stack() and bpf_get_task_stack() pass\nmay_fault=true into the common stack collection code. Resolving user-space\nbuild IDs may then call build_id_parse_file() and block on filesystem\nreads.\n\nNeither helper prototype sets might_sleep. Since prototype selection uses\nthe sleepability of the whole program, the verifier can still allow these\nhelpers from a non-sleepable region within that program, such as an\nexplicit RCU or preemption-disabled region. The task-stack helper can also\nbe called from a non-sleepable timer callback of a sleepable program.\n\nMark both faultable prototypes as sleepable. The existing helper context\ncheck then rejects these calls while continuing to allow them in genuinely\nsleepable contexts.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44b8d370f2725bad215da3e67668e98ba96671bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3014e8a8bdad55075d89836ad9c10710a9a69837", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19e8d5a98afd071d8c1c5adeccf92b3c42eddc70", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d02927fdf4e930893c92e35fed01a2704496900"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x3f6-2q7c-8rc9", "CVE-2026-98045"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b50cc83-80d1-369d-90f7-bd2542348335", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "267c36bf-b935-3129-8e74-43234db09815", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "2ae68c0a-473b-32cd-ac27-dd7cc6beaf7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4dd9775ec242425576af93daadb80a34083a53c <44b8d370f2725bad215da3e67668e98ba96671bd"}, {"id": "376f8af5-380a-30f6-b194-aa62d097005a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4dd9775ec242425576af93daadb80a34083a53c <3014e8a8bdad55075d89836ad9c10710a9a69837"}, {"id": "658f72f1-e07f-36b1-9166-4da4709c62be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "70f5b14b-b8bd-359b-9af0-8cae31179d73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "71ca8695-0c69-3656-9f57-0ca016aed277", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4dd9775ec242425576af93daadb80a34083a53c <9d02927fdf4e930893c92e35fed01a2704496900"}, {"id": "780002ad-92b5-30a2-816b-ec63ad303248", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "c03efd5e-e158-3fcc-81dd-798b51ea5545", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4dd9775ec242425576af93daadb80a34083a53c <19e8d5a98afd071d8c1c5adeccf92b3c42eddc70"}, {"id": "f42c3d6b-a106-3108-aadc-b6fc0e91b63b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5585e739-2c5a-39b3-9b61-ee40aeda7ddc", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}